#!/usr/bin/env bash
# pre-push — SINGLE-WRITER GUARD for tap main (XACA-1122-023).
#
# CANONICAL SOURCE (XACA-1170-005): this file is authored in dev-team at
# scripts/templates/tap/tap-single-writer-pre-push.sh. sync-tap.sh mirrors it to
# .githooks/pre-push in the TAP repository (DoubleNode/homebrew-aiteamforge) and
# the armed publisher ships it post-merge. Edit THIS copy, never the tap copy
# (XACA-0340: a tap-side edit is reverted by the next mirror). It is NOT the
# outer dev-team .githooks/pre-push — that is a different file with a different
# job (XACA-1122-007).
#
# ── WHAT IT ENFORCES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Refuse any push to the tap mainline that does not originate from either:
#   (a) the serialized post-merge publisher running in GitHub Actions, or
#   (b) a sanctioned release cut driven by scripts/kb-tap-release.
#
# Everything else — most importantly a human or agent running
# `./sync-tap.sh --commit` inside the shared ~/dev-team/homebrew-tap checkout and
# then pushing by hand — is refused.
#
# ── WHY THE THIRD WRITER IS THE POINT ─────────────────────────────────────────
# XACA-1122's decision of record says "because there is exactly one writer to tap
# main, a second writer cannot exist." Traced mechanically that was NOT true.
# THREE writers survive: the publisher, kb-tap-release, and a hand push.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-09: plain `./sync-tap.sh` (and `--commit`) never pushes; it
# commits both sides and stops, telling a HUMAN to push. (Its `--publish` mode,
# added later for the publisher, DOES push -- `git -C "$TAP" push "$TAP_REMOTE"
# "HEAD:${TAP_BRANCH}"` -- and only the publisher should run that.)
# Removing the gitlink from feature PRs does not remove that capability. The
# shared tap checkout is exactly where such a push originates, and it produced
# three distinct cross-session hazards in one week (XACA-1122 subitems 017/019/
# 020/022).
#
# ── SCOPE: MAINLINE ONLY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fires only for pushes whose REMOTE ref is the tap mainline (refs/heads/main).
# Side branches, tags, and every other ref are untouched — pushing a topic branch
# to the tap stays as easy as it is today. Deleting or force-updating main IS in
# scope, because both are writes to main.
#
# ── HONEST LIMITS — DO NOT OVERSELL THIS HOOK ─────────────────────────────────
# 1. IT IS ADVISORY. `git push --no-verify` skips every pre-push hook, and the
#    allow-signals below are environment variables that any local caller can set.
#    A determined or careless local actor defeats it. That is inherent to hooks,
#    not a defect in this one.
# 2. IT IS PER-CLONE AND OPT-IN, WHICH IS NOT WHAT XACA-1122-023 WAS BRIEFED.
#    MEASURED 2026-09-09: `core.hooksPath` for the tap resolves from
#    file:/Users/darrenehlers/dev-team/.git/modules/homebrew-tap/config — it is
#    LOCAL REPOSITORY CONFIG. Git never transports config as content. Proven with
#    a fixture: a clone of a repo that has a tracked .githooks/pre-push AND
#    core.hooksPath=.githooks comes back with core.hooksPath EMPTY and its
#    effective hooks dir at .git/hooks. So committing this file ships the FILE to
#    every clone but NOT its ACTIVATION. The tap's own .githooks/README.md agrees,
#    calling these hooks "Opt-in", and docs/LOCKSTEP-CHECK.md records that
#    "Existing machines must be done by hand."
#    => Coverage is exactly: clones where someone set core.hooksPath (or installed
#       the global init.templateDir dispatcher). That INCLUDES the shared
#       ~/dev-team/homebrew-tap checkout, which is the highest-risk site and the
#       origin of the recorded incidents. It does NOT include an arbitrary fresh
#       clone.
# 3. THEREFORE THIS HOOK IS THE SECOND LAYER, NOT THE FIRST. Server-side push
#    restriction on tap main is the mechanism that cannot be bypassed locally.
#    See homebrew-tap-staged/docs/protection/README.md (dev-team, reference only) for the exact
#    command, and for the reason it needs enforce_admins=true to bind at all.
#
# ── WHY IT CANNOT SELF-BLOCK THE PUBLISHER (verified, not assumed) ────────────
# Two independent reasons, either of which alone is sufficient:
#   (i)  actions/checkout performs a fresh clone, so core.hooksPath is unset and
#        git looks in .git/hooks — this file is never consulted. MEASURED above.
#   (ii) even if a workflow deliberately sets core.hooksPath, the publisher
#        context is an explicit ALLOW branch below.
# Note also what this hook deliberately does NOT do: it never resolves
# dev-team/develop, never fetches the outer repo, and never reads the mirror map.
# Its predicate is pure identity, evaluated from the environment. That removes the
# entire class of "cannot resolve the outer repo from a CI clone" failure.
# (The XACA-0848 ordering guard that once complemented it was retired in XACA-1580.)
#
# ── ONE HOOK PER CLONE, NO INSTALL STEP (XACA-1580) ───────────────────────────
# This file is the only pre-push hook for a tap clone. It used to be a dispatcher
# that also chained a per-clone <hooks-dir>/pre-push.local (the retired XACA-0848
# ordering guard, installed by a script). Tap main is single-writer server-side
# now, so that second stage, its install step and its missing-hook WARNING are gone.
# A leftover pre-push.local is simply never consulted.
#
# ── EXIT CODES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   0 — allowed: out of scope, publisher, sanctioned release cut, or override
#   1 — REFUSED: unsanctioned writer
#   2 — REFUSED: cannot determine scope (malformed stdin). Distinct from 1 so
#       "could not judge" is never confused with "judged bad" — but BOTH block.
#   There is no silent-pass exit. A guard that allows on "I could not check" is
#   the fail-open shape this repo has shipped before and must not repeat.
#
# ── ESCAPE HATCH ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_OVERRIDE=1 git push        # loud, audited in the log
#   Prefer this over --no-verify: --no-verify disables EVERY hook and leaves no
#   trace that a guard was bypassed.
#
# ── ENVIRONMENT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_OVERRIDE  "1" => allow, loudly (emergency)
#   TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_RELEASE   "1" => sanctioned release cut (set by
#                               scripts/kb-tap-release; see XACA-1122-008)
#   TAP_MAIN_BRANCH             tap mainline branch name   (default: main)
#   TAP_PUBLISHER_WORKFLOW      publisher workflow name    (default: Tap Publisher)
#   TAP_PUBLISHER_REPOSITORY    owner/repo the publisher runs in
#                               (default: DoubleNode/dev-team)
#
# ── PORTABILITY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bash 3.2 compatible (no associative arrays, no mapfile, no `local -n`) so it
# runs on stock macOS /bin/bash as well as CI bash 5.

set -eu

SELF="tap-single-writer"
ZERO_SHA="0000000000000000000000000000000000000000"
TAP_MAIN_BRANCH="${TAP_MAIN_BRANCH:-main}"
MAIN_REF="refs/heads/${TAP_MAIN_BRANCH}"
PUB_WORKFLOW="${TAP_PUBLISHER_WORKFLOW:-Tap Publisher}"
PUB_REPO="${TAP_PUBLISHER_REPOSITORY:-DoubleNode/dev-team}"

say()  { echo "[${SELF}] $*"; }
warn() { echo "[${SELF}] $*" >&2; }

# ── 1. Emergency override, checked first so it works even when nothing else can
if [ "${TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_OVERRIDE:-0}" = "1" ]; then
  warn ""
  warn "  ***************************************************************"
  warn "  *  WARNING: TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_OVERRIDE=1                      *"
  warn "  *  SINGLE-WRITER GUARD BYPASSED for tap ${TAP_MAIN_BRANCH}"
  warn "  ***************************************************************"
  warn ""
  warn "  You are pushing to the tap mainline outside the publisher and outside"
  warn "  a release cut. If a publisher run is in flight this can interleave with"
  warn "  it and strand consumers. Verify nothing else is writing before you"
  warn "  continue, and say why in the commit message."
  warn ""
  exit 0
fi

# ── 2. Scope — is the tap mainline among the refs being pushed?
# git feeds pre-push one line per ref on stdin:
#   <local ref> <local sha> <remote ref> <remote sha>
# A missing/empty stdin means git had nothing to push; that is not a write.
TOUCHES_MAIN=false
SAW_LINE=false
DELETING_MAIN=false

while read -r local_ref local_sha remote_ref remote_sha || [ -n "${local_ref:-}" ]; do
  [ -z "${local_ref:-}" ] && continue
  SAW_LINE=true
  # Malformed line: we cannot tell what is being written. Fail CLOSED.
  if [ -z "${remote_ref:-}" ]; then
    warn "ERROR: malformed pre-push input line: [${local_ref} ${local_sha:-} ${remote_ref:-} ${remote_sha:-}]"
    warn "Cannot determine whether tap ${TAP_MAIN_BRANCH} is being written. Refusing."
    exit 2
  fi
  if [ "$remote_ref" = "$MAIN_REF" ]; then
    TOUCHES_MAIN=true
    [ "${local_sha:-}" = "$ZERO_SHA" ] && DELETING_MAIN=true
  fi
done

if [ "$SAW_LINE" = false ]; then
  exit 0
fi

if [ "$TOUCHES_MAIN" = false ]; then
  exit 0
fi

# ── 3. ALLOW: the serialized post-merge publisher, running in GitHub Actions.
# All three signals are required. GITHUB_ACTIONS alone is not enough — any CI job
# in any repo sets it, and this guard is specifically about the tap publisher.
if [ "${GITHUB_ACTIONS:-}" = "true" ] \
   && [ "${GITHUB_REPOSITORY:-}" = "$PUB_REPO" ] \
   && [ "${GITHUB_WORKFLOW:-}" = "$PUB_WORKFLOW" ]; then
  say "publisher context (${PUB_REPO} / ${PUB_WORKFLOW}) — allowing push to ${TAP_MAIN_BRANCH}."
  exit 0
fi

# ── 4. ALLOW: a sanctioned release cut.
# scripts/kb-tap-release sets TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_RELEASE=1 inline on its tap push
# (XACA-1122-008). A release cut is a legitimate second writer, serialized against
# the publisher by the lock ref, NOT by this hook.
if [ "${TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_RELEASE:-0}" = "1" ]; then
  say "sanctioned release cut (TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_RELEASE=1) — allowing push to ${TAP_MAIN_BRANCH}."
  exit 0
fi

# ── 5. REFUSE.
warn ""
warn "  ==============================================================="
warn "  REFUSED: unsanctioned push to tap ${TAP_MAIN_BRANCH}"
warn "  ==============================================================="
warn ""
if [ "$DELETING_MAIN" = true ]; then
  warn "  You are attempting to DELETE ${MAIN_REF}."
else
  warn "  Only two writers may push to the tap mainline:"
  warn "    1. the serialized post-merge publisher (GitHub Actions)"
  warn "    2. a release cut via scripts/kb-tap-release"
fi
warn ""
warn "  This push is neither. The most common way to reach this message is"
warn "  running ./sync-tap.sh --commit and then pushing by hand. A plain"
warn "  ./sync-tap.sh run does not push -- it commits and asks you to -- and that"
warn "  manual step is exactly the third writer XACA-1122 exists to remove."
warn "  (./sync-tap.sh --publish does push; it is the publisher's mode, not yours.)"
warn ""
warn "  WHAT TO DO INSTEAD"
warn "    * Mirrored content: let the publisher ship it. Merge your canonical"
warn "      change to dev-team/develop; the publisher pushes the tap half and"
warn "      bumps the gitlink, in that order, under a lock."
warn "    * Cutting a release: use scripts/kb-tap-release, which sets"
warn "      TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_RELEASE=1 and takes the lock. Never hand-roll the commit"
warn "      and tag — a hand-cut subject also trips tap-changelog-completeness."
warn "    * Genuine emergency: TAP_SINGLE_WRITER_OVERRIDE=1 git push"
warn "      (loud and audited; preferred over --no-verify, which silently"
warn "      disables every hook)."
warn ""
exit 1
